  9046	
  9047	### 12.2 Git workspace schema
  9048	
  9049	The Git wire schema is the exact <code>kind = git</code>
  9050	<code>WorkspaceSnapshotMember</code> and its closed nested types in Section
  9051	10.4. There is no second prose-only Git descriptor. In particular,
  9052	<code>head</code> distinguishes branch, detached, and unborn states;
  9053	<code>object_pack</code> and its inventory carry offline object closure; the raw
  9054	<code>index</code> blob plus logical <code>GitIndexEntry</code> array preserve
  9055	stages and flags; <code>working_tree_manifest_id</code> carries actual tracked,
  9056	unstaged, untracked, and explicitly included ignored bytes; and submodule,
  9057	feature, cwd, and agent-config fields are all required members of that same
  9058	Transfer Manifest object.
  9059	
  9060	Remote URLs MUST be sanitized. User info containing a password/token, credential
  9061	helpers with embedded secrets, and machine-local paths MUST be removed.
  9062	Repository config MUST be reconstructed from an allowlist: remotes, branch
  9063	tracking, object format, safe submodule URLs, and required worktree extensions.
  9064	Hooks, credential configuration, local include files, and arbitrary commands
  9065	MUST NOT be copied.
  9066	
  9067	The <code>WS-GIT-ROUNDTRIP-1</code> and
  9068	<code>WS-TREE-ROUNDTRIP-1</code> fixtures in Section 10.4 are normative inputs
  9069	to <code>AC-WORK-001</code>/<code>AC-WORK-002</code>. An implementation MUST
  9070	parse those exact descriptors before invoking Git or writing a destination;
  9071	it MUST reject their listed negative mutations without relying on a live
  9072	repository to fill missing schema facts.
  9073	
  9074	### 12.3 Git capture and materialization
  9075	
  9076	Capture MUST quiesce agent input and filesystem-mutating provider work. It MUST
  9077	read Git state consistently and fail if HEAD, index, or included file digests
  9078	change during capture.
  9079	
  9080	Materialization MUST:
  9081	
  9082	1. create or validate a managed repository/worktree;
  9083	2. configure sanitized remotes;
  9084	3. import each repository's object pack into that repository's object database
  9085	   only and verify its required OIDs there; a superproject gitlink is validated
  9086	   against the child descriptor/pack, never by co-mingling child objects into
  9087	   the parent database;
  9088	4. establish the exact branch or detached HEAD without contacting a remote;
  9089	5. construct a temporary index from the descriptor and atomically install it;
  9090	6. materialize actual working-tree bytes, modes, and symlinks;
  9091	7. recurse through submodules using their logical mappings; and
  9092	8. compare resulting HEAD, index, status, cwd, and content digests with the
  9093	   descriptor.
  9094	
  9095	An implementation MAY use the Git executable, a Go library, or both, but the
  9096	observable result is fixed by this section. Unsupported Git extensions, case
  9097	collisions, inaccessible filters, or object-format mismatches MUST fail closed.
  9098	Network fetch MAY be offered as an explicit repair, but materialization MUST NOT
  9099	silently depend on it.
  9100	
  9101	Staged and unstaged states are distinct: the reconstructed index represents the
  9102	staged version, while the working-tree manifest represents actual working
  9103	bytes. A clean-looking working tree with a wrong index is a failed
  9104	materialization.
  9105	For a submodule, the superproject HEAD-tree pointer, stage-0 index
  9106	<code>gitlink_oid</code>, and checked-out <code>head.oid</code> MUST reproduce the
  9107	exact clean/staged/unstaged combination in Section 10.4.
