+# Git workspace capture axis inventory — TASK-260830-2xt6fd
+
+## Measured entry points
+
+The capture coordinator is `(*tmuxserver.Lifecycle).CaptureGitWorkspace` in
+`internal/tmuxserver/capture_git_workspace.go`. It composes the landed status,
+quiesce-input and wait-safe-boundary operations with
+`gitsnap.AssembleProvisional`. The component entries remain `gitsnap.Capture`
+(with `ContentOptions`) and `gitsnap.AssembleProvisional`; component
+tests do not substitute for the coordinator tests.
+
+| Gate / axis | Generated or boundary domain | Production entry and evidence | Structural argument and explicit bound |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Terminal Instance state at capture admission | All eight closed states: absent, creating, parked, active, quiescing, stopped, stale_fenced, unavailable | `CaptureGitWorkspace`; `TestCaptureStopPointStateDomain`; accepted quiescing/stopped paths in `TestCaptureGitWorkspaceQuiescedAssemblesAndRechecks` and `TestCaptureGitWorkspaceStoppedAssemblesWithoutBoundary` | Only quiescing with same-incarnation input-closure and provider boundary receipts, or stopped, is admitted. No release/restore operation is called. |
+| Terminal Instance state after assembly | Same eight states | `CaptureGitWorkspace`; `TestCaptureFinalStatusStateDomain` | The final status and incarnation are re-read after assembly; a transition out of the stop-point states refuses. |
+| Quiescence evidence kind and generation | Missing receipt, stale incarnation, checkpoint-only proof, provider quiescence, provider process exit | `CaptureGitWorkspace`; `TestCaptureProviderProofRequirements`; `TestCaptureRejectsCheckpointBoundaryAsProviderProof` | The coordinator asks the landed owner for `wait-safe-boundary`, validates its durable receipt and generation, and does not create its own state machine. |
+| Unix socket absence observation | Existing parent + absent socket, absent parent, `ECONNREFUSED`, and unclassifiable errors | `UnixDialer.Dial`; `TestUnixDialerMissingSocketIsStale`, `TestUnixDialerMissingDirectoryIsUnknown`, `TestUnixDialerLiveStaleUnknown` | Only a missing socket under an existing directory or `ECONNREFUSED` is stale; missing parent and failed parent reads remain unknown. `N-unix-dialer-missing-parent-admits-stale` is killed by `TestUnixDialerMissingDirectoryIsUnknown`. |
+| Custody ancestor path depth through production entries | Generated extra depth 1..16 × three ancestor positions × Probe/Spawn/Execute = 144 cases; separate physical walk reaches PATH_MAX | `Probe`, `Spawn`, `Execute`; `TestCustodyAncestorWalkGeneratedDepthAtProductionEntries`, `TestCustodyAncestorWalkGeneratedDepthToPathMax` | `checkCustodyAncestors` walks parents until filesystem root without a fixed hop cap. `CheckSocketLength` bounds paths that reach the production custody walk. `shortTestTempDir` relocates a `t.TempDir()`-owned directory under canonical `/var/tmp` so fixture names do not consume the socket path budget. |
+| Repository identity name | 1..256 Unicode characters; the tests exercise 1, 256, and 257 plus multibyte identities | `Capture`; `TestEdgeIdentity256CharsAccepts`, `TestEdgeIdentity257CharsRefuses`, multibyte identity case in `bounds_edge_test.go` | `utf8.RuneCountInString` enforces the character bound. At most 1,024 UTF-8 bytes follow from the 256-rune cap; this is not a byte-counted contract. |
+| Relative path grammar and depth | Generated invalid forms include empty, absolute, drive-prefixed, NUL, backslash, encoded separators, and empty/dot/parent segments; accepted fixture paths use multiple segments | `Capture` / `AssembleProvisional`; `TestCaptureRefuses...` family in `internal/gitsnap`; scalar path tests; `TestAssemblyRecursiveCWDAndConfigClosure` | `scalar.ParseRelativePath` iterates the input segments and sets no AX character/depth maximum. Actual filesystems impose component/path limits. No test claims arbitrary OS path depth or byte length; these are reported bounds. |
+| Manifest entry count | 0..65,536 accepted; 65,537 refused | `Capture` and canonical manifest validation; `TestManifestEntryCountBoundary` in `internal/canonicaljson/manifest_entries_test.go`; `TestEdgeIndexMaxAccepts` / `TestEdgeIndexMaxPlusOneRefuses` for Git index capture | The canonical JSON owner supplies the common schema count gate; gitsnap does not fork it. Canonical encoded-object size is an independent 5 MiB limit. |
+| Git index entry count | Generated boundary 65,536 / 65,537 | `gitsnap.Capture`; `TestEdgeIndexMaxAccepts`, `TestEdgeIndexMaxPlusOneRefuses`; canonical JSON `TestGitIndexEntryCountBoundaryIsBoundBelowThePublicObjectSizeGate` | Count equality is also checked against the parsed entry array. No large-index throughput guarantee beyond the boundary fixtures is claimed. |
+| Workspace member count and topology | 1..256 members; 1,024/1,025 tree-fanout switch | `AssembleProvisional`; `TestAssemblyMultipleMembers`, `TestAssemblyManifestFanout` | Member count is checked before assembly. The fan-out fixture measures graph construction only, not 1,025 live repositories. |
+| Recursive submodule count/depth | Total 256/257 boundary; depth refusal at `depth >= 16`; nested live fixture reaches two levels | `Capture`; `TestContentSubmoduleCountBounds`, `TestContentNestedDetachedSubmodule`, recursive assembly cases | Traversal increments a shared count and checks depth before descent; cycles are tracked by active Git directory. Depth 16/17 is structurally bounded but not exhaustively generated as 17 nested real repositories. |
+| Symlink target name bytes / characters | Target is valid UTF-8, 1..4,096 characters; escaped, absolute, separator and invalid targets have refusal coverage | `Capture` with `ContentOptions`; `TestContentSymlinks`, `TestContentSymlinkChainsAndExcludedTargets`, `TestContentDigestRaceAndRetry` | AX measures characters. Worst-case UTF-8 target is 16,384 bytes. Target payload sizes across all Unicode scalars are not exhaustively enumerated. |
+| Symlink chain hops | 0..40 accepted; 41 refused | `Capture` with `ContentOptions`; `TestContentSymlinkChainBoundaryAtProductionCapture` | `safeSymlink` iterates pending path components and rejects on hop 41; visited filesystem cycles eventually repeat or hit the same 40-hop cap. The test constructs 40 and 41 hop chains through `Capture`. |
+| Pack object count / inventory | Each imported pack's count and object inventory are compared to the pack header and exact `rev-list` inventory; object count has no package-specific finite cap | `AssembleProvisional`; `TestAssemblyPackIndexAndBytes`, `TestAssemblyRecursivePacks`, `TestAssemblyFailedReadsAndCorruptObjects`, `TestAssemblyIsolatedDatabaseIgnoresAmbientObjects` | Count and OID membership are checked from production Git output and imported bytes. The loop is linear in Git's exact inventory and bounded by memory, storage, Git and OS resources. No million-object throughput or maximum-pack-size success claim is made. |
+| Git refs/remotes/filter names | Ref name 1..1,024 bytes; remote count 1..16; required filters 0..64 | `Capture`; `TestCaptureRequiredFilterCountBounds`, ref/remotes bounds tests, and `TestAssemblyOptionsAndUnsupportedSources` | Ref byte length is an explicit scalar limit; remote and filter counts are schema bounds. Other names are bounded by their corresponding schema/string owner. |
+| Object bytes and descriptor closure | Blob size 0..128 GiB; chunk size 4 MiB; descriptor, blob, raw index and pack identities are cross-checked | `AssembleProvisional`; `TestAssemblyPackIndexAndBytes`, `TestValidateProvisionalClosureAndDescriptors`, `TestAssemblyCrashAfterObjectsAndRetry`, `TestCaptureProcessCrashRetry` | The chunked blob writer checks observed bytes against declared size and digest. No 128 GiB throughput claim is made; pack/index assembly still materializes bytes in memory. |
+| Crash/retry phases | Crash at pack phase (exit 74) and after assembly before closing status (exit 75), then same durable-state retry | `CaptureGitWorkspace`; `TestCaptureProcessCrashRetry`; assembly store retry tests | The crash matrix is two named durable interruption points, not every machine instruction. A failed process may leave immutable unreferenced objects; retry re-observes sources and verifies/reuses immutable bytes. |
+
+## Evidence bounds
+
+- Repeated closing observations detect persistent source changes, not a change
+  that occurs and is completely reverted between reads. The held terminal and
+  provider quiescence is the protection during the interval.
+- Git's external execution and host filesystem are trusted; arbitrary filter
+  sandboxing and cross-platform runtime equivalence are not proved here.
+- Arbitrary Git destination materialization, checkpoint publication, doctor
+  capability advertising, group-history selection/conflict resolution, and a
+  live-session capture that returns to active are outside this leaf's contract.
+- OS-specific maximum path depth/bytes and scale behavior above the stated
+  generated boundaries remain bounds, not inferred guarantees.
